WEBVTT

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.420
I slept in!

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>It's getting some incredible hype.</i>

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.440
<b>Tourism economy booming in city 
where popular anime Galtan is set</b>

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.440
<b>Galtan's economic effects on the town of Oarai</b>

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.540
<i>It's having an amazing effect on the economy.</i>

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.750
Morning!

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.250
Morning, Minoa.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.080
Jeez, why didn't anyone wake me up?

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.660
I did.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.830
And you were like...

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.010
"Asagaya Minoa is now awake, sir!"

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.590
"Ready for action, sir!"

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.550
Was I?

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.590
It's what always happens, though.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.990
Why didn't you wake me up again, then?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.930
You're taking it pretty easy today.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.940
We don't have morning practice today.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.140
What about you, Mii-chan?

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.970
Aren't you going to join a club or anything?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.620
Not really.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.190
I'm not like Onee-chan.
I'm not athletic or anything.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.200
What about an arts club?

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.780
An arts club?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.410
It's okay, Mii-chan.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.410
You've been the type to play inside your 
room rather than outside, even as a kid.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.420
Onee-chan, did I watch
 anime when I was little?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.420
I think you did.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.890
<i>Haritaro</i> and <i>Dezumon</i> and all that.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.830
I watched <i>PreFae</i> with you.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.430
Thanks for the meal.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.470
<i>PreFae</i>, huh?

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.810
That's not it.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.630
I'm leaving.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.580
Minoa, let's go to the station together.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.040
I'm going to be late.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.450
Morning.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.740
Erika! Give me a ride!

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.340
Nope. Double riding is illegal.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.880
Go Sakaneko!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.440
Go! Go!

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.940
Morning.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.340
Morning.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.690
Morning, Minocchi.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.160
Morning, Kouenji-san.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.570
Good morning.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.470
What are you reading?

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.970
That's a title?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.080
"<i>A Certain</i>..."

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.010
<i>A Certain Report on the Irresponsible 
and Depressing Chronicles</i>

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.080
<i>of Me and a Certain Eccentric 
Childhood Friend</i>.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.590
Th-That sounds complicated.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.700
It's not complicated.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.800
It's about a pathologically tardy protagonist

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.590
and their time-wasting childhood friend.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.700
O-Oh, yeah?

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.490
M-Morning.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.750
Good day.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.400
Sh-She's so cute.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.000
I love the way she's just 
slightly condescending.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.430
Morning, Kamiigusa-san.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.680
Good day.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.290
Morning, Minoa.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.370
Morning.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:57.010
Something about Kamiigusa-san?

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.420
Nah, she just seems so flawless, 
I don't know how to approach her.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.030
From what I've heard, she's...

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.510
Sebas!

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.430
Well done.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.440
She's <i>really</i> well-to-do.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.390
Yeah, I totally get that.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.190
I saw your morning practice.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.320
I can't improve my time.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.950
Hey, what made you decide 
to join the track club?

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:35.270
I saw a broadcast of the Olympics 
when I was in elementary school.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.710
I was awed by the female athletes.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:41.710
I wanted to be able to run like them.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.340
You were moved as a child, huh?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.950
Don't you have anything like that, Minoa?

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.110
Do you watch anime, Yui-chan?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.970
Anime?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.200
Not really, I guess.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.700
Yeah?

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.590
Was there an anime that moved you as a kid?

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.980
Not so much moved, but there's 
one that I'm curious about.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.420
What's it called?

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.960
That's the thing. I don't know.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.990
There's the bell.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.960
Morning, everyone.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.640
Good morning.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:19.520
Well, it's been almost a month 
since the entrance ceremony.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.750
Are you enjoying high school life?

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:28.190
Oh my, you're so quiet.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.760
I'm feeling lonely.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.190
Roppongi-sensei's so colorful.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:37.510
He's like that at track practice, too.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.360
<i>Phone call for Gomon-sensei.</i>

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.400
<i>Please come to the staff office.</i>

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.780
You're buying bread on top of your bento box?

00:07:56.980 --> 00:08:00.210
You burn up a lot of calories 
when you're in track.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.460
Oh yeah, my sister eats a lot, too.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.770
Asagaya-san...

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:05.540
Yes?

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.550
K-Kamiigusa-san!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.800
Her aura's amazing,
even during lunch break...

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.720
May I have a word with you?

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:15.360
Yes.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.430
I need to talk to you.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.430
Would you kindly spare me 
some time after school?

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.280
Talk?

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.460
I'll be waiting at the art room show hall.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.190
I ask you to come alone.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.740
Um...

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.940
What are we...

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.190
Understood?

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:33.450
What are we talking about?

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.170
I'll see you there.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.270
Did she get called out?

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.110
Does she have her eye on her?

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:47.130
Did I do something wrong?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.840
D-Dunno...

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.210
<b>Verb usage</b>

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.350
There's a 70% chance this 
is going to be on the exam,

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.320
depending on my mood that day.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.350
That's it for homeroom.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:02.140
<i>The budgeting committee meeting 
will be beginning at 4 PM today.</i>

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:01.470
Class committee, could you give me a hand?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:06.230
<i>All club presidents, please assemble 
at the student committee office.</i>

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.010
Want me to come with you?

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.990
It's okay, you should go to your club.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:16.870
But...

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.370
She asked me to come by myself.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.360
You dropped something.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.720
Watch it!

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:34.560
You must be careful about 
touching that grimoire.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.550
Grimoire?

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.400
Abracadabra, pasta la vista!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.020
It's safe to touch now.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.060
I set up a barrier.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.300
R-Right.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.540
Danke schön.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:54.820
Danke?

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:02.580
People don't really come here.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.700
That's why I called you here.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.480
I'm glad you came.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.840
Um...

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.840
What did you want to talk to me about?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.490
Answer my questions honestly.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.340
Understood?

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:34.070
<b>Minoa,
 Anime Rookie!</b>

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.280
Asagaya Minoa-san...

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.400
Y-Yes?

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:48.910
Do you like anime?

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:50.030
What?

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.920
Do you like anime?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.380
Anime?

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:58.050
You were asking Obata-san this 
morning if she watches anime.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.930
Oh, yeah...

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.800
What are you watching this season?

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:02.640
This season?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.560
I personally like <i>Hero School</i> and <i>Ru:ZERO</i>.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:08.750
I have big hopes for <i>Shikabari</i>, 
the original anime, too.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.350
The <i>Time Travel Shounen</i> OP is legit, too.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.190
Jun-nii's stylish fence jump!

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:15.410
Shikabari?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:21.420
Oh, maybe we don't have any taste overlap.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:22.910
Are you into slice-of-life, then?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.070
Overlap? What?

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:27.090
This season's kind of lopsided, honestly.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.190
Too many battle anime.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.960
<i>Tamukeda</i> and <i>Toramiko</i> are about 
the only slice-of-life shows.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.150
Oh, <i>Bakusou</i>?

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.210
Nah, that's a bike show pretending 
to be a slice-of-life show.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:38.880
Oh, I dabble in delinquent stuff, though.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:42.820
They're a bit old,
but <i>Kyou Kara Sessha Wa!!</i> and <i>Angel Story</i>...

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.470
Wait, both are OVAs.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:46.630
There's a remake boom happening now, though.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:50.100
I wonder if they're going to make an anime
 based on <i>The Guy Who Dances With Bad Luck</i>?

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.800
Huh?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.650
That's not it, either?

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:56.070
Oh, do you like otome stuff?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.940
Or hardcore robot anime?

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.990
You were talking about anime, weren't you?

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.790
No, I, uh...

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.830
I watched a normal amount of anime as a kid.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.240
<i>Gachiemon</i> and stuff.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.680
<i>Gachiemon</i>!

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.830
Nobue? Karashi?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.250
Which movie did you like?

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.250
I liked <i>Chijipara Suikoden</i>.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.650
A lot of people online like the 70s version,

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:21.010
but I swear, the 2000s version has way 
better character design than the original.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:24.760
I'm sorry, who's Nobue?

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.770
Forget everything I just said.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.900
I never knew you liked anime, Kamiigusa-san.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.330
You really don't look like the type.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.020
Is there a problem with that?

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:44.030
No, I got the sense that 
you <i>really</i> like anime.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.030
You were talking really 
enthusiastically just now.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:53.790
I thought you were more unapproachable.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.190
Unapproachable?

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:57.420
Perhaps.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.170
I wish you'd always talk like you just did.

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:03.920
Good day.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:04.980
Wait!

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:09.180
It's true that there's an anime I've been 
curious about ever since I was little.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:15.560
But I can't remember which anime it was.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:18.560
You seem to know a lot.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.070
Maybe you'd know which one it is.

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.700
Describe a scene to me.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:29.340
A robot stands up, and a 
girl transforms and sings,

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:31.250
and they fly up into the sky with an angel.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.610
That's it?

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.330
That's it.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.470
But I have dreams about it, too.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:40.840
It must have been really moving to me.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.030
Standing. Transforming. Singing.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.750
Into the sky with an angel. Moving.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.880
It might be the final episode 
of <i>Espoir no Shoujo Kaiji</i>.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.770
Nope.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:01.600
<i>A Dog of Decadence</i>.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.700
This is <i>the</i> show about
 angels and going into the sky.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.460
The last episode was so sad!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.360
I cried so hard.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:08.990
That's not it.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.340
<i>Cinnamon Roll Z</i>.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.420
<i>Previous Genesis Everstrike</i>.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.240
<i>Autumn Wars</i>.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.000
I don't think that's it.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.010
Are you sure it's an anime?

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.130
I'm certain.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.480
I don't have enough information.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.570
Maybe if I knew what 
happens before or after.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.560
I wonder if I'm remembering wrong.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:32.570
I apologize for not being of assistance.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.230
I'm sorry, too.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:37.020
I don't know too much about anime.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.140
It's all right.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:43.560
I know! We just need to go where there are 
a lot of people who are familiar with anime.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.530
Wait, where are we going?

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.910
Don't most high schools have an Anime Club?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:55.540
Let's see, fine arts, 
Japanese cultural history,

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:58.040
provincial art, tea...

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.740
If you're looking for the Anime Club, I...

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.080
Don't you want to talk more about anime?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.050
Don't you want to have more 
fun talking about anime?

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.290
Well...

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:15.680
Light music club, classical 
literature club, NJ club...

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:19.810
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:19.810
I found it, the Anime Club!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.690
Asagaya-san, that room...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.910
Come on!

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.190
Hello?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:30.680
Huh?

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:34.830
The Anime Club isn't active.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.960
I looked it up on the day 
of the entrance ceremony.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.060
Oh.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.940
It's not active?

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:50.650
I wonder if they still have a room.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.090
Wh-What?

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:58.060
Th-This is the first issue
of <i>Anime Shangri-La</i>!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.100
Is that one of those anime magazines?

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:04.860
Anime Shangri-La

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.220
It's a treasure!

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:04.860
Anime's amazing.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:10.640
I mean, it lets me see you 
make all kinds of faces.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.490
Stop that.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.800
I'm sure the Anime Club would be fun.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.970
But what's the use if it isn't active?

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.620
Just start one.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.070
You could do it.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.380
Start one?

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.930
Just recruit some members.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:30.880
There are so many students at school.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:35.310
There's no way you're 
the only anime fan here.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.890
Maybe, but...

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:37.660
Right?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:38.770
You should do it.

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:41.150
I'll help you find members.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.380
But...

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:46.390
I like seeing you talk about anime.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:47.650
Asagaya-san...

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.370
You have to take the initiative.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.440
Yeah.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.150
You might be right.

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:55.490
Of course I am.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.490
I'll do it.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.020
Yup.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.980
We have to make an official submission 
to the student committee.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.250
I think we need a minimum of six members.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:07.750
You'll find five more in no time.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.390
You're right.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.510
I've already found one.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.700
Me and you.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.190
We just need four more.

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:17.470
Um...

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:21.050
I'll help you find members, 
but I'm not joining.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:24.020
We're putting up recruiting flyers tomorrow.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:29.020
I told you, I don't really know enough 
about anime to join an Anime Club.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:36.740
I'll lend you just a small selection 
of beginners' anime from my library.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.660
A selection?!

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.850
<i>The Girl who Slept Through Time</i> and <i>Replica</i>.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.160
They're movies, so they shouldn't 
take more than two hours each.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.670
<i>This is getting complicated...</i>

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.170
Anyway, let's clean this room up.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.020
Does that door lead to a storage room?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.190
I'll go to the student council and 
borrow a key if they have one.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:08.560
Okay.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:17.700
It's open.

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:21.270
Hey!

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:22.160
What...

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.640
It opened.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:33.330
And why is there a cat inside?

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.080
A beret?

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.100
I asked, but they don't 
have a key for that door.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.940
Oh, it's open?

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.080
Yeah, it opened.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.070
So it wasn't locked, then?

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:55.260
A cat?

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.030
How did it get in?

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.760
The door was closed.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:02.330
It might have wandered in through 
the air ducts or something.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:03.580
Oh, right.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.330
Over here, kitty.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:11.080
What a hostile cat.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:23.190
Now that it's clean,
 let's go home for the day.

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.820
I need you to watch that.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:28.680
Let's go.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.310
Bye, kitty.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.020
Now, we're going to be busy tomorrow.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.630
We're going to start handing out
 flyers from before 8:00 AM.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.820
Don't you dare be late.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.100
Um...

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.920
Just to make sure, am I—

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:48.890
You're a member.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.260
Of course.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.190
Huge.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:57.450
I-Is this your ride, Kamiigusa-san?

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.140
It's huge.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.560
Your car's huge.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.320
See you tomorrow.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:03.130
Yeah.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.600
See you.

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:07.350
Asagaya-san...

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:11.940
Thanks.

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:15.190
I look forward to working with you.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:18.690
Same.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.200
Good day.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.570
I hope we find members soon.

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:27.320
We will.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:30.370
We'll find those of the same mind as us.

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:36.670
Of the same mind as us?

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.340
Well, all right.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.260
I wonder who's going to join.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.970
<b>God's Love on This
Wonderful Blessing!</b>

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.500
I finally got that rare, 
exclusive merchandise!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.060
<b><i>Maria Clara</i></b>

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.060
<b>Anime Announced!</b>

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.810
Nakano-senpai!

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.310
Senpai!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:57.850
Bye-bye.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:15.920
It's so windy!

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:25.290
Huh?

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.160
It's gone.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.370
Crap, I think I left my phone at school.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.440
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.490
It's gone!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.250
Where did I leave it...

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:43.820
Ow!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.570
So you're the "clumsy girl" type.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:47.410
Who's there?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.410
Is this what you're looking for?

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.160
The cat...

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:58.680
It's talking!

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:35.840
Remakes get lame after a while.

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:38.550
Next episode, we find out who the caller was.

00:23:38.550 --> 00:23:40.280
Don't drop us after the first episode.
